Rule 1: Never use 'as any'
❌ const data = res.json() as any;
✅ const data = UnknownSchema.parse(await res.json());

Rule 2: Prefer Discriminated Unions over optional properties
❌ type State = { loading?: boolean; error?: string; data?: User };
✅ type State = { status: 'loading' } | { status: 'success'; data: User } | { status: 'error'; error: string };

Rule 3: Always handle Promise rejections explicitly.
